# Build context: app/vote
#
# This file did not exist before, which is why the Dockerfile's "COPY . ." copied
# whatever happened to be in the directory. See docs/arch/application.md, defect D7.
#
# This is an allow-list, not a deny-list. Everything is excluded first, then the few
# files the image actually needs are added back. A deny-list silently ships anything
# nobody thought to exclude; an allow-list fails visibly instead.
#
# Maintenance rule: a new file or directory that the image needs must be added here
# in the same commit. The symptom of forgetting is an ImportError or a 404, not a
# silent leak.

*

!Dockerfile
!requirements.txt
!app.py
!static
!templates
